# Integer128 division by zero

Divides 100 by zero to verify the failure surfaces as a language-level
division-by-zero error with exit code 1 instead of producing a value.

>>> source
dividend: int128 = 100
divisor: int128 = 0

quotient: int128 = dividend / divisor
print(quotient)

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: division by zero

<<< exit
1
